  "resource_label": "Annual household resources after modeled taxes, excluding health benefits; includes SNAP, WIC and other noncash benefits valued by the model. Housing/utility expenses affect benefit rules but are not subtracted from this resource measure.",
  "assumptions": [
    "All members hold US citizenship and citizen SSN cards and live together in Harris County, Texas throughout 2025. Memberships remain constant throughout the year.",
    "One unmarried male adult heads the tax unit and household. The parent has a 4-year-old dependent daughter. Each person has a separate marital unit. The scenario stipulates filing status without establishing legal eligibility.",
    "The parent earns $30 per hour over 52 weeks. Annual earnings of $33,650\u2013$33,850 and the corresponding weekly hours vary together at 201 paired points. The child has no earnings or work hours.",
    "The household pays $12,000 annual rent, $1,800 electricity, $600 telephone and $360 water separately. Electricity provides heat and cooling. Other utility bills and paid childcare cost $0. The scenario supplies no formula-owned childcare expense output.",
    "The adult owns $1,000 in bank assets; the child owns $0. Stocks, bonds and other assets total $0. The input-only SPM-unit asset measure totals $1,000. Debt may finance a low-earnings housing-budget shortfall; the scenario imputes no additional income.",
    "The scenario sets listed input-only nonwage income facts to $0. Remaining primitive monetary inputs use model zero defaults; the scenario supplies no calculated tax base or benefit award.",
    "Neither person has employer health insurance or a disqualifying offer. They do not buy ACA coverage. They claim Medicaid/CHIP if eligible; formulas determine enrollment. Resources exclude health benefits under the unchanged baseline.",
    "Members claim SNAP and EITC if eligible. They do not claim cash TANF; TANF eligibility and SNAP income formulas remain live. The scenario assumes no housing-assistance allocation or Head Start placement and sets those take-up inputs to false. It overrides no eligibility or final award.",
    "The child has a hypothetical, independently stated WIC nutritional-risk assessment and claims WIC if eligible. The adult has no pregnancy, disability, blindness or college-student status.",
    "Formulas calculate the parent's child-age exemption from SNAP work requirements.",
    "We request 2025 inputs and calculations; native structural selection defaults to 2024. These illustrations do not certify every 2025 legal branch or a 2017 comparison."
  ],
